AJAX Database Example:

- AJAX can be used for interactive communication with a database.

#) AJAX Database Example:
    - The following example will demonstrate how a web page can fetch information from a database with AJAX:
        
        1️⃣ ASP.NET Core as a server:
            - Let's implement AJAX for fetching Expenses from the existing project ExpenseTracker

                👉 server endpoint for getting list of expenses from backedn project ExpenseTracker:
                    
                    http://localhost:5167/api/v1/expenses?page=1&pageSize=15&sortBy=Date&sortDesc=true
                
                👉 Backend CORS Config:

                    options.AddPolicy("FrontendPolicy", policy =>
                    {
                        policy
                            .AllowAnyHeader()
                            .AllowAnyMethod()
                            .AllowCredentials()
                            .WithOrigins("http://127.0.0.1:5500"); //💡frontend URL(live server URL of ajaxDB.html )
                    });

                👉 Frontend html: (ajaxDB.html)

                    <body>
                        <p id="promptOp"></p>
                        <button onclick="myPrompt()">Save new token</button> <br><br>
                        <button onclick="loadExpenses()">Load Expenses</button>
                        <p id="ajaxOp"></p>
                        <script>

                            // 💡ajax
                            function loadExpenses(page = 1) {

                                const token = localStorage.getItem("token"); // or wherever you store it

                                const xhttp = new XMLHttpRequest();

                                xhttp.onload = function () {
                                    if (this.status === 200) {
                                    const data = JSON.parse(this.responseText);

                                    let html = data.items.map(e =>
                                        `<li>${e.id} : ${e.title} - ${e.amount}</li>`
                                    ).join("");

                                    document.getElementById("ajaxOp").innerHTML = `<ul>${html}</ul>`;
                                    } else {
                                    document.getElementById("ajaxOp").innerHTML = "Unauthorized or error, save a new JWT Token first and Try again!";
                                    }
                                };

                                xhttp.open(
                                    "GET",
                                    `http://localhost:5167/api/v1/expenses?page=${page}&pageSize=15&sortBy=Date&sortDesc=true`
                                );

                                // Authentication 
                                xhttp.setRequestHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " + token);

                                xhttp.send();
                            }

                            // 💡using prompt to get the JWT Token from user
                            function myPrompt() {
                                document.getElementById("ajaxOp").innerHTML = "";
                                let text;
                                let jwt = prompt("Please enter a new JWT token");
                                if(jwt == null || jwt == "") {
                                    text = "You cancelled the propmt.";
                                } else {
                                    // call function to save the entered JWT Token.
                                    saveToken(jwt);
                                    text = "JWT Token saved."
                                }
                                document.getElementById("promptOp").innerHTML = text;
                            }

                            // 💡function to save the JWT Token
                            function saveToken(jwt) {
                                localStorage.setItem("token", jwt);
                            }
                        </script>
                    </body>

                👉 Run the server and login to get the JWT Token. Run the frontend html in live server.

                
            🧠 Explanation:
                👉 we used prompt to get the JWT Token from user, prompt function myPrompt() calls the
                    saveToken() function to save the token in browser's local storage.
                👉 Inside the ajax function, first we retrieve the saved token from browser's local storage.
                    Backend/server is returning JSON, not HTML so we need to parse the returned data to convert
                    raw string onto JS object

                        const data = JSON.parse(this.responseText);
                
                👉 Then we transform data into HTML:

                        let html = data.items.map(e =>
                            `<li>${e.id} : ${e.title} - ${e.amount}</li>`
                        ).join("");
                    
                        💡data.items → array from backend
                        💡.map() → loops through each expense
                        💡builds HTML string per item
                        💡.join("") → combines into one string
            
